1e:["$","section",null,{"children":[["$","$L16",null,{"label":"Empathize Phase","title":"Understanding the","accent":"Workflows"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","$L33",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-4 font-semibold text-ink","children":"Qualitative research"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink/70","children":"Research here was stakeholder-led rather than survey-led: the people who understood each workflow were the branch teams operating it. Each session was a walkthrough of the current process in their own words — what arrives, who handles it, where it waits, and which questions they end up answering by phone. Reconstructing those workflows out loud is what exposed the failure shared across every module: the system held the status, but only a person could release it."}]]}],["$","$L17",null,{"className":"flex flex-col justify-center","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 text-[15px] font-bold text-[color:var(--accent)]","children":"Research approach"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-6 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink/65","children":"Stakeholder-led rather than survey-led. Working sessions with the branch teams who operated each module day to day, walking their real process step by step instead of asking them to describe it in the abstract."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-2 gap-4","children":[["$","div","Modules covered",{"className":"rounded-sm border border-ink/12 bg-ink/[0.035] p-4 text-center","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"t-metric text-[color:var(--accent)]","children":["$","$L38",null,{"value":"5","delay":0}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-[11px] text-ink/60","children":"Modules covered"}]]}],["$","div","Stakeholders each",{"className":"rounded-sm border border-ink/12 bg-ink/[0.035] p-4 text-center","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"t-metric text-[color:var(--accent)]","children":["$","$L38",nul